# hunting-grounds-ambush.vrs: hunting-grounds D23 (Session 2). hg-ambush (AroundPlayer 20-30 m, scope FarbaneWoods, the
# lock on, one wave of 4 CHAR_Spider_Forest): with Chaos at the pond, inside Farbane, the start spawns 4 around Chaos;
# with Chaos at (-1680, -1080), in DunleyFarmlands, the same start skips the wave "no eligible player".
# Needs: the step 3 Release DLL; NyarDevTools (.devtp, .devgo, .devmark, .devhop) and DevChatEcho; the dev events.json
# entries hg-roam, hg-lock, hg-ambush, hg-point, hg-timing (docs/features/HUNTING_GROUNDS.md, Session 2), scope
# FarbaneWoods (the pond is in it, Session 1); [Debug] VerboseLogging = true; Chaos invulnerable
# (`ToggleInvulnerable true`, a Boolean, never false).
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .devgo pond
expect-log \[DEV TP\] pond
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
chat .nyar region here
expect-reply you are in FarbaneWoods
mark
chat .nyar event start hg-ambush
expect-log event hg-ambush wave 1/1 around a player: 4 units queued timeout=30
wait 6
chat .nyar debug here 40
expect-reply CHAR_Spider_Forest hg-ambush
shot full hg-ambush-in
chat .nyar event stop hg-ambush
expect-log event hg-ambush stopped
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
chat .devtp -1680 -1080
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 3
chat .nyar region here
expect-reply you are in DunleyFarmlands
mark
chat .nyar event start hg-ambush
expect-log wave 1 of hg-ambush skipped: no eligible player timeout=30
wait 5
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0
chat .nyar event stop hg-ambush
wait 2
